---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Simplified sound values for display. Old Turkic distinguishes front/back
// consonant variants (b¹/b², etc.) — this table shows the variants used in
// this site's decoration. Worth a fact-check pass before publishing.
const glyphs = [
	{ glyph: "𐱅", sound: "t", note: "the mark in the site header" },
	{ glyph: "𐰋", sound: "b", note: "front-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰚", sound: "k", note: "front-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰠", sound: "l", note: "front-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰃", sound: "i / ï", note: "vowel" },
	{ glyph: "𐰏", sound: "g", note: "front-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰼", sound: "r", note: "front-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰽", sound: "s", note: "back-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰴", sound: "q", note: "back-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰆", sound: "o / u", note: "vowel" },
	{ glyph: "𐰖", sound: "y", note: "back-vowel variant" },
	{ glyph: "𐰭", sound: "ŋ", note: "as in 'song'" },
];
---

<!-- Site B · glyphs — the page that explains the theme. -->
<BaseLayout
	title="Glyphs — Tarik Duyar"
	description="Why there's a 1,300-year-old alphabet on this site: a short tour of Old Turkic script."
	bodyClass="bg-[#0a0b0d] text-gray-200 antialiased"
>
	<div class="bg-[#0d0e12] border-x border-[#90c5ff14] max-w-5xl mx-auto min-h-dvh">
		<nav class="py-5 px-6 md:px-12 border-b border-[#90c5ff14] sticky top-0 bg-[#0d0e12]/90 backdrop-blur-sm z-40">
			<div class="flex justify-between items-center">
				<a href="/12" class="flex items-center gap-3">
					<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/70 text-lg leading-none select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
					<span class="font-sinistre text-xl text-white">Tarik Duyar</span>
				</a>
				<ul class="flex gap-5 md:gap-7 text-sm">
					<li><a href="/12/writing" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Writing</a></li>
					<li><a href="/12/resume" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Resume</a></li>
					<li><a href="/12/glyphs" class="text-white underline decoration-blue-400/50 underline-offset-4">Glyphs</a></li>
					<li><a href="mailto:atduyar@gmail.com" class="text-blue-300 border border-blue-500/30 px-3 py-1 hover:bg-blue-600/10 hover:border-blue-400/50 transition-all">Contact</a></li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main class="px-6 md:px-12 py-14 max-w-3xl">
			<header class="mb-12">
				<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/40 text-4xl block mb-6 select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐰋𐰃𐰠𐰏</span>
				<h1 class="font-sinistre text-4xl text-white mb-4">Why there are runes on my website</h1>
				<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					Every glyph decorating this site is a real letter from a real alphabet —
					not fantasy runes. Here's the story.
				</p>
			</header>

			<div class="space-y-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-14">
				<p>
					In the Orkhon Valley of today's Mongolia stand stone monuments from the
					early 8th century — the <span class="text-white">Orkhon inscriptions</span>.
					They're the oldest known written texts in any Turkic language, carved in
					an alphabet now called Old Turkic script. As someone from Türkiye, this
					is the earliest written form of the language family I grew up speaking.
				</p>
				<p>
					I keep the script around my site for a specific reason. Those
					inscriptions are <span class="text-white">thirteen-hundred-year-old
					documentation that is still readable</span>. The kingdoms that
					commissioned them are gone; the message survived because it was carved
					carefully, in a clear structure, on durable material. Most software
					doesn't survive a single decade. It's a good bar to aim at.
				</p>
				<p>
					The script reads right to left, has separate consonant variants for
					front and back vowels (a feature Turkish phonology still has), and was
					deciphered in 1893 by Vilhelm Thomsen — using "Türk" and "Tengri" as
					crossword-style cribs.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Interactive glyph table -->
			<section class="mb-14">
				<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-white mb-2">The letters on this site</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">Hover or tap a tile to see its sound.</p>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-6 gap-3">
					{glyphs.map((g) => (
						<button type="button" class="glyph-tile group relative border border-[#90c5ff14] hover:border-blue-400/50 bg-[#0a0b0d]/50 aspect-square flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-1 transition-all cursor-pointer focus:outline-none focus:border-blue-400/70" data-note={g.note}>
							<span class="font-oldturcic text-3xl text-blue-300/80 group-hover:text-blue-200 leading-none transition-colors select-none">{g.glyph}</span>
							<span class="text-xs text-gray-600 group-hover:text-gray-400 transition-colors">/{g.sound}/</span>
						</button>
					))}
				</div>
				<p id="glyph-note" class="text-sm text-blue-300/80 mt-4 min-h-5 transition-opacity">&nbsp;</p>
			</section>

			<!-- The site mark -->
			<section class="mb-14 border border-[#90c5ff14] bg-[#0a0b0d]/50 p-8">
				<div class="flex items-start gap-6">
					<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-300 text-6xl leading-none select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
					<div>
						<h2 class="font-sinistre text-xl text-white mb-2">The site mark</h2>
						<p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
							The letter in the header is /t/ — for Tarik. The longer sequence
							in some footers, <span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-300/80">𐰋𐰃𐰠𐰏</span>,
							spells <em>bilig</em>: "knowledge, wisdom" — one of the most common
							words in the inscriptions, and a decent one-word mission statement
							for a personal site.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-10">
				Sound values shown are simplified; the script's front/back consonant pairs
				are collapsed here for readability. Corrections welcome —
				<a href="mailto:atduyar@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">atduyar@gmail.com</a>.
			</p>

			<footer class="pt-8 border-t border-[#90c5ff14] flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-4 text-xs text-gray-600">
				<a href="/12" class="hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">← home</a>
				<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/20 tracking-[0.3em] select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐰋𐰃𐰠𐰏</span>
			</footer>
		</main>
	</div>

	<script is:inline>
		const note = document.getElementById("glyph-note");
		for (const tile of document.querySelectorAll(".glyph-tile")) {
			const show = () => { note.textContent = tile.dataset.note; };
			tile.addEventListener("mouseenter", show);
			tile.addEventListener("focus", show);
			tile.addEventListener("click", show);
		}
	</script>
</BaseLayout>
